    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's first define what the complement of an angle is. The complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in a right angle (90 degrees).\n\nLet's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the measure of this angle is double its complement. The complement of \\( x \\) degrees is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees. Therefore, the angle \\( x \\) is double this value:\n\n\\[ x = 2 \\times (90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, we will solve this equation step by step.\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right-hand side:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to isolate \\( x \\):\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees.\n\nTo verify, let's check if this angle is indeed double its complement. The complement of \\( 60 \\) degrees is \\( 90 - 60 = 30 \\) degrees. Twice \\( 30 \\) degrees is \\( 60 \\) degrees, which matches the measure of our angle.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{60} \\]",
